<ArticleLayout slug="shoot-it-or-generate-it" ctaLabel="Talk to the production team">
  <p class="standfirst">Most advice on this splits the world into believers and holdouts. The useful version is narrower. There are four conditions that force a camera, and once you can name them the rest of the catalog stops being an argument.</p>

  <h2>When should you shoot a product and when should you generate it?</h2>

  <p>Shoot when the asset has to prove something physical, when a regulator or a marketplace requires the real item, when a real person appears, or when scale is the point. Generate the variants, the environments, and the repetitions around those anchors. hubStudio runs most ecommerce catalogs at about 70 percent generated and 30 percent shot, and the interesting question is which 30 percent stays in front of a camera.</p>

